# The real configuration names a database and a workspace and is per
# deployment. surface.example.toml is the one that is committed.
surface.toml

# Secrets never live here. The database URL arrives through the
# environment; this line exists so that a .env created for local work
# cannot be committed by accident.
.env
*.env

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Design iteration screenshots, taken while the front end was being
# argued about and kept only until the thing they compared was settled.
#
# THIS LINE IS WHY THE PARENT REPOSITORY KEPT REPORTING THIS SUBMODULE AS
# MODIFIED. git reports a submodule dirty when it has untracked content,
# so eleven leftover jpgs in here showed up in VFM's own `git status` as
# a modified `brightbean-surface` — which reads exactly like a stale
# gitlink, and was misdiagnosed as one for most of a day.
#
# Measured rather than assumed, with `git status --porcelain=v2`: the
# flags were `S..U` — untracked only, NOT commit-changed and NOT
# tracked-modified — and the recorded and actual commit shas were the
# identical 1c48fdd. The pointer was correct the whole time.
#
# NOTE THE ASYMMETRY, so that nobody later "corrects" it: the parent
# repository TRACKS its own control/design-evidence/, 68 files that are
# the card-by-card design review somebody asked for and may want again.
# These are intermediate iterations of pages that have since been agreed.
# Same directory name, opposite treatment, deliberately.
/design-evidence/
